Package: kelixip-mod-captioning
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: Emmanuel BUU <emmanuel.buu@ives.fr>
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Section: net
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://www.ives.fr/
Depends: kelixip (= @VERSION@)
Description: Correction service of a captioned call, for kelixip
 Answers the captioning INFO a client sends during a call placed by
 call-captioning.exs and hands it the
 URL of a correction stream on the speech-server, with a single-use token
 minted on the speech-server's control API. Renewals are bounded per call, and
 the token is masked in every log and trace. Enable it with a
 [module.captioning] block in config.toml.
 .
 The payload is BEAM bytecode, but the package is architecture-dependent on
 purpose: it must be built and shipped alongside the core whose embedded ERTS
 will load it.
